<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 552 or 553</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teia was the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, elected after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/totila">Totila</a>'s death at Taginae in 552. He gathered the remaining Gothic forces and marched south to protect the Gothic treasure at Cumae, but was trapped near Vesuvius by the Byzantine army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narses">Narses</a>. He was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mons-lactarius">Battle of Mons Lactarius</a>, after which organised Gothic resistance collapsed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teia.jpg" alt="Teia" width="144" height="137" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Regno_dei_goti,_teia,_emissione_bronzea,_552-553.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
